b3508319c8191a1ec2a42e35aec34","call_id":"call_7967b220602348508cdccea93d30e91e","name":"submit_artifact","arguments":"{\"artifact_json\":\"{\\\"target_review\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"PASS\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"The original exercise as contextualized in source-context.md asks for every prime p, field K of characteristic p, integer 0≤lambda<p, and arbitrary admissible lattice M, with V(K)=M⊗_Z K irreducible as L(K)-module. spec.json full_target and H001–H004 preserve these quantifiers and the arbitrary-lattice scope; the conclusion spells out nonzero and invariant-subspace irreducibility. No restriction to a selected lattice, exclusion of p=2 or lambda=0, or distinct-weight assumption is introduced. The stated edge cases are included in the target. However, the proof supplied for this target has a blocking inference defect recorded in structure_review/findings.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"problem.md:3\\\",\\\"source-context.md:14-45\\\",\\\"spec.json:4-5,24-44\\\"]},\\\"definition_reviews\\\":{},\\\"source_reviews\\\":{},\\\"structure_review\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"FAIL\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"Graph has the four frozen H roots and one R001 producer directly outputting P; there are no D or M propositions and no source applications to review. The single inference is not mathematically sufficient. In R001 S002, the claimed matrix-unit identity X_(lambda-i) E_(lambda,lambda)=E_(i,lambda) is false in general: on e_lambda, the supplied S001 formula gives coefficient binom(2(lambda-i),lambda-i), not 1. For example lambda=2,p=3,i=0 gives coefficient 6, which is not a unit in Z_(3) and is zero after reduction mod 3. Consequently the stated conclusion that every matrix unit is in the R-algebra generated by divided powers does not follow. S003 depends on those matrix units preserving M_R, and S005 depends on the resulting matrix units acting on the reduction; those steps are not established. Thus AND-closure to P fails. This is an inference-body mathematical review finding, not a claim that the target theorem is false. No per-inference packet replay is claimed.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"nl0.json:72-85 (R001 graph edge)\\\",\\\"nl0.json:359-387 (S001-S002)\\\",\\\"nl0.json:408-445 (S003 and F001)\\\",\\\"nl0.json:479-499 (S005)\\\"]},\\\"findings\\\":[{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"FAIL\\\",\\\"location\\\":\\\"nl0.json R001 S002, followed by S003 and S005\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"With r=lambda-i, X_r e_lambda=binom(r+r,r)e_(lambda-r); hence X_(lambda-i)E_(lambda,lambda)=binom(2(lambda-i),lambda-i)E_(i,lambda), not the claimed matrix unit. At lambda=2,p=3,i=0 the factor is 6, noninvertible in R=Z_(3) and zero modulo p. The asserted matrix-unit generation, the use of it to obtain coordinate projections on M_R, and the irreducibility argument from E_(j,i) therefore lack support. This is a defect in the supplied proof route; no corrected proof is supplied.\\\"},{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"UNVERIFIED\\\",\\\"location\\\":\\\"signature-evidence.json:1; nl0.json propositions and applications\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"There are no M proposition IDs or source applications in the candidate, so M source-fidelity/applicability scope is inapplicable. signature-evidence.json is empty. No source theorem is silently reviewed or treated as a premise.\\\"},{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"UNVERIFIED\\\",\\\"location\\\":\\\"nl0.json:5-70,72-508; spec.json:46-114\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"There are no global D definitions; definition_reviews is empty. R001 introduces local definitions and objects rather than declared D objects. Their legitimacy/use is not a substitute for the failed inference, and this Audit A requested summary is blocked by that defect.\\\"}]}\"}","status":"completed"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[{"type":"function","name":"search_mathlib","description":"在固定 mathlib 的 Lean 源码中搜索正则表达式，返回至多 100 行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_mathlib","description":"读取固定 mathlib 中一个 Mathlib/...lean 文件的指定行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start_line":{"type":"integer"},"line_count":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start_line","line_count"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_task_input","description":"Read an explicitly frozen task document by ID; no other local files are accessible.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["id","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_yui","description":"Read declared Yui rules/templates; no tests, historical runs or personal files.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_artifact","description":"Check a JSON artifact against the explicit stage contract; this is not automatic mathematical certification.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_artifact","description":"Submit a JSON artifact after its stage checks.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"report_obstacle","description":"Stop this stage honestly on a substantive or suspected proof gap, unavailable source, or input conflict. JSON fields: status, location, explanation, basis, partial_progress. Status must be SUBSTANTIVE_GAP, SUSPECTED_GAP, SOURCE_UNAVAILABLE or INPUT_CONFLICT. 